A||||6||Fformula88||Free Flow Catalytic Converter?||||5||
Z||000000||Fformula88||05-06-2000||11:26 AM||||I need a new cat converter... the old one is plugging up my exhaust and causing many problems.... I was wondering if it would be better to get a free flow converter instead of a stock replacement to open up the exhaust a bit more... maybe get a bit more power out of the car.  I still have the remaining parts of the exhaust stock (original in fact... they sure last long time!)  Thanks!||||reg||5
Z||000001||KnightRyder31||05-06-2000||11:37 AM||||Sound like a good idea to me. Opening the cat should give a bit more power, not much but some is better than none. And it would breath much better.<BR>Good luck  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>----Knight----<BR>           ||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||05-06-2000||02:40 PM||||My cat is as free-flowing as they come.  All it needed was a little sawing and a long screwdriver.||||reg||1
Z||000003||phillip||05-06-2000||05:14 PM||||i had one put on when i switched to dual exhaust (4cyl.). can't really tell any difference but since i needed one and want to some day do an engine upgrade i went with it in hope of needing it in the future.||||reg||1
Z||000004||mutfish||05-06-2000||09:32 PM||||Not too long ago I replaced the melted converter with one made by Catco Inc.,it was listed as a "high flow" piece.The exhaust was a little louder,but I don't really know if it flows any better than the rest.....||||reg||1
Z||000005||mutfish||05-06-2000||09:40 PM||||Oh yeah, by the way,let's not be "guttin'" the converters.Have you ever driven behind a car without one? What if everybody did that?<BR>It is NOT going to get you any appreciable street performance.........<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fformula88||05-07-2000||04:37 PM||||Thanks for all the advice!  I think I'll get a free-flowing cat... maybe it will increase performance, maybe not.  At least it will not sputter and stall when the exhaust clogs itself!||||reg||6
